From: ththeod <2376818+ththeod@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 02:10:28 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 137/138] W4A8-INT8 Marlin: signed group scales (int16, not
 uint16) + abs-max normalization; INT8 MoE debug log

Merlin-quantized checkpoints (Swift/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next) fold a sign into
~50% of the group scales. marlin_act_int8_process_scales normalized by the
max (not abs max) and the INT8 kernels read the int16 scales as uint16, so
every negative scale became ~65K: ~20,000x error, garbage output (W45/W46).
Read them as int16 in the MoE and dense Marlin templates (needs a rebuilt
_moe_C; the in-tree .so is rebuilt for sm_80/86, prebuilt kept as
*.prebuilt) and normalize by the absolute maximum.

Also VLLM_E2_INT8_MOE_DEBUG=N: log inputs, scales and outputs of the first N
non-zero prefill-sized MarlinExperts calls per process (default off).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
